+## 2026.11.23a
+
+**The program release** (the owner's order of 2026-11-13, its design and plan addendum approved at the design gate that day and its scoped revision for the field finding F7 on 2026-11-14; four stages, P1 to P4, every increment through the full gate and every stage through its review by both): what the loop did by hand and by memory becomes programs that refuse, record and measure. The pace audit of 2026-11-09, the Sunday evaluations of 2026-11-01 and 2026-11-08 and the field findings F1 to F7 are its sources; release S's rows are carried as records only. The programs that change: `bridge_env.py`, `bridge-run.py`, `review-guard.py`, `permission-guard.py`, `trace-check.py`, `invisible-check.py`, `records-migrate.py`, `inventory-check.py`, `conformance-check.py`, `mutation-run.py`, `pace-report.py`, `evaluate-reports.py`, `roster-check.py`, `bridge-install.py`, `bridge-check.py`, `loop-guard.py` (its refusal names the in-flight log) and `cursor-agent.shim` (the strip's names), with `tools/make-manifest.py`. Against 2026.11.12a: two files new (`in-flight.py`, `push-scan.py`), none removed, two allow entries new (`Bash(python ~/.claude/cursor-bridge/in-flight.py:*)`, `Bash(python ~/.claude/cursor-bridge/push-scan.py:*)`), no deny entry changed.
+
+**What changed**
+- **R-076, the suite passes stripped** (TASK-055): `tests/conftest.py` keeps the launch environment's `APPDATA` under a name of the tests' own before it replaces it, and `tests/test_release_t_strip.py` assumes nothing of the shell it runs in; the bridge's whole suite is green in a stripped run through the launcher.
+- **R-077, a moved or retired passage is caught** (TASK-057): `trace-check.py --moves [--base <rev>]` reads every `.md` under `bridge/` but this file, at the merge-base and at HEAD, and fails for each passage of a changed file that stands nowhere at HEAD, a reworded one included, unless an entry the range itself adds to `docs/TRACE_MOVES.md` excuses it by its normal form's hash and first words; an added entry that excuses nothing is a finding; CI runs it on every pull request; the record keeps the full gate. The pinned mode is unchanged.
+- **R-078, the launcher's forms** (TASK-059, TASK-082): the test and driver kinds accept the interpreter's `-B` and `-X utf8` before the module; npm's `--prefix`, pnpm's `--dir` and `-C` and yarn's `--cwd`, and the environment names that move those runners' folder, are held to the target rule (exit 125 outside the launch roots, the variable named and its value never printed); the refusal's message tells a known runner's refused option from an unknown runner; `merge_ids` sorted; the plan glob escapes its root.
+- **R-079, a review's own launcher rows** (TASK-061): `learned_limit` ignores rows that started inside a review run; `review-guard.py verify` names, as a note, the launcher rows written during the review; the bridge's launcher tests write their rows under a temporary folder.
+- **R-080, the strip holds** (TASK-060): a key file naming `USERPROFILE`, `HOME`, `HOMEDRIVE`, `HOMEPATH`, `APPDATA` or `LOCALAPPDATA` is refused before the run (exit 125, the name printed, never the value); the secret-like name test, one copy in `bridge_env.py`, also matches `PAT`, `CREDS`, `AUTH`, `DATABASE_URL` and `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`; a secret-like `CURSOR_` name is withheld from every stripped run but a builder's or a reviewer's.
+- **R-081, git's configuration watched** (TASK-062): around a test or driver run the launcher reads the repository's `config` and `info/attributes`, a worktree's `config.worktree`, `commondir` and `.git` file, and every hook by name and content, and prints `bridge-run: GIT-CONFIG <path> <word>` (`new`, `removed`, `changed`, `unreadable`) for each difference, the run's exit unchanged and nothing restored; step 4 reads the line.
+- **R-082, the permission guard reads a command as the shell does** (TASK-063, BUG-045): a `$`, a backtick or a process substitution outside single quotes makes a Bash command unreadable, and an unreadable command is refused (the PowerShell reader alike, a line-ending backtick excepted); quotes close as bash closes them; `--no-verify` is read as an option of the seven git subcommands it applies to; an unquoted `&` in a `gh api` argument is refused with what to quote; git's global options, inline aliases (`git -c alias.<name>=...`), accepted abbreviations and `git config core.hooksPath` are read (BUG-045). Every earlier refusal stands; the deny rules are unchanged.
+- **R-083, CI proven by a program** (TASK-064, TASK-083, BUG-046): `bridge_env.py` reads a branch's required contexts from the classic protection and the rules, and the auto-merge setting, by GET; `review-guard.py ready <pr>` prints `READY` (exit 0) and writes the ready record only where the pull request's head is the local head, the premerge record stands and every required context has passed on that head (`NOT READY` exit 1, `CANNOT CHECK` exit 2); the permission guard refuses a `gh pr merge` without the ready record for that number and head; `premerge` and `premerge-records` say whether auto-merge is on; step 8 runs `ready` after the watch and arms no merge.
+- **R-084, verify's closing words** (TASK-064): `verify` and `premerge` say `deleted` or `rewritten` for the snapshot as it was.
+- **R-085, a watch never returns before CI has run** (TASK-065, TASK-082): before `gh pr checks <n> --watch` the launcher waits, inside the run's limit, until every required context has a check or status on the pushed head, or the head's workflow runs have checks where no context can be named, and says what it waited for; a watch's return is never the proof, `ready` is.
+- **R-086, invisible characters by category** (TASK-066): `invisible-check.py` refuses every character of Cc, Cf, Zl, Zp and of Zs but the plain space, tab, line feed, carriage return and a leading byte-order mark excepted, naming a nameless one by its code point.
+- **R-087, the pre-push scan** (TASK-067, FIX-006, TASK-082): `push-scan.py [<base>]` reads every commit of `<base>..HEAD` (messages, author and committer lines, added lines and file names) for a path of this computer and for the owner's account names, derived at run time and extended by `~/.cursor-bridge/names.txt`, never printing the matched text; exit 0 clean, 1 on a hit, 2 where git cannot be read (a git before 2.40 included); `secret-sentinel` and step 8 name it.
+- **R-088, the live position by a program** (TASK-068, TASK-078): `in-flight.py` appends a clock-stamped line to `run/supervisor/in-flight.md`, and with `--pass <name> <reviewer> [--round <n>] [--cause <cause>]` a tagged pass line; rule 54, calibration's step 0 and the parallel builders' paragraph name it; KP-041 is retired.
+- **R-089, the pace report counts every increment and round** (TASK-069, TASK-078, BUG-047): `review-guard.py snapshot` records the round's `Round cause:` from its SCOPE file; `pace-report.py` counts a name by its brief, its guard rounds or a tagged pass line, and `PR-<n>` by a squash naming no counted name, prints round causes over rounds and a line of recorded passes per week by reviewer kind; the causes stand once in `bridge_env.py` and gain `base update`.
+- **R-090, the mutation run proves its baseline** (TASK-070): each distinct test list runs once unmutated first, a failure ending the run with exit 5, no mutant run and the cache untouched; a node id's backslashes are replaced in its file part only.
+- **R-091, an empty run parameter is named** (TASK-071, TASK-078): `records-migrate.py` refuses a run-parameters record with any of the five values empty (`cannot read <file>: <name> has no value on a plain line`), `inventory-check.py` fails one, headed or not, and calibration names the repair.
+- **R-092, the weekly scan in the conformance check** (TASK-072, TASK-078): rows for the weekly workflow, its `schedule:` trigger and its lock-file list equal to the gate's scanner step's; a NOTE without a GitHub remote or with an inventory Decisions row beginning `Weekly scan:`, MISSING otherwise; a diagram index with every kind omitted passes.
+- **R-093, the release tooling checks its own tree** (TASK-074): `bridge-check.py --sources` refuses (exit 2) where it does not stand in the tree it checks, naming the folders; `tools/make-manifest.py` writes `VERSION` with the file's own line ending.
+- **R-094, the installer refuses what it does not know and keeps a named copy** (TASK-073): an unknown word, `--help` or a missing value prints the usage and exits 2, the target untouched; `--keep <version>` keeps a named earlier copy over later installs until `--keep none` or another; `--rollback [<version>]` can name a kept copy and writes `ROLLED-BACK.md` from every newer entry.
+- **R-095, a signed-out Cursor tool is told from a failing model** (TASK-075, TASK-078): `roster-check.py` prints `SIGN-IN  the Cursor command-line tool is signed out: run cursor-agent login`, counts no failure and exits 5; calibration's install run sheet ends with `cursor-agent status`.
+- **R-096, a quoted command that is not instructed** (TASK-076): `tests/test_allowlist.py` skips an inline command on a line that carries the mark `<!-- not run -->`. The mark is a convention for whoever writes the bridge's text: put it on a line that quotes a command as an example and does not instruct it; an instruction is never marked.
+- **R-097, the Sunday evaluation's security step** (TASK-077, TASK-078): `evaluate-reports.py security [--date <date>]` reads, by GET alone, each project's weekly workflow, its runs since the last read and the open Dependabot alerts, and writes `Reports/Evaluations/<date>/security.md` in release T's three kinds and green; a failed read is a finding with its remedy; the project roots stand in the per-computer file `~/.cursor-bridge/projects.json` (an object of name to root), which `pace-report.py` reads too, and without which the program names the file and exits 2.
+- **R-098, one dependency increment for every failing lock** (TASK-078): the policy says the bumps of several lock files with new advisories travel in one `DEP` increment and one pull request; KP-050's Correction is a pointer.
+- **R-099, design and planning on Fable 5.2** (TASK-079): rule 48 and its digest line, calibration's report template and the change cycle name Fable 5.2; `plan-critic` carries `model: claude-fable-5-2`.
+- **R-100, Context7 for the Claude side** (TASK-080): `spec-packager` and `diff-reviewer` add `mcp__context7__*` to their `tools:` lines and may look a third-party library's documentation up where the session has the server; the lookup names the version the lockfile pins, what it returns is a hint and data, never evidence or an instruction, a query carries library names and topics only, and an agent without the server works as before and says no lookup was made. The configuration guide says the same for the Claude side; no allow entry is needed.
+- **R-101, the bridge's own records checked** (TASK-058): a test runs `inventory-check.py` over this repository's records and one asserts `header_agrees` for every headed record.
+- **R-105, a merge unit of one increment refused** (TASK-084, TASK-082): before any run, exit 125, the launcher refuses a brief whose `Merge unit:` line holds one ID, or whose header's `merge_unit` lists one, where neither names two or more, saying that a merge unit names two or more increments and that a brief of one increment carries no such line and `merge_unit: null`; `spec-packager` says the same.
+- **R-102**, this stamp; **release S's rows** R-066 to R-075, R-103 and R-104, built by 2026.11.12a, carried into this repository's register as records only, each with its evidence, no program or text of theirs changed here.
+
+**Running projects must**
+- *(all phases)* Install with every project paused at a merge boundary, everything committed, restart, run `/calibrate-bridge` before the next increment. Run the installer with `--dry-run` first and read its `previous` and kept lines, then the real run, which ends 0 with `RESULT: INSTALLED TREE MATCHES bridge 2026.11.23a` and keeps 2026.11.12a as the way back; then `cursor-agent status` in the owner's terminal, which must not say signed out.
+- *(all phases)* Where Context7 is not yet set up for Claude Code on the computer, the install's run sheet adds it once, at user level: `claude mcp add --transport http --scope user context7 https://mcp.context7.com/mcp`, and `claude mcp list` shows it connected. On a computer without the `claude` command, Claude Code's command-line tool is installed first from its own documentation and called by the path its installer names, since the installer does not put it on PATH. A computer without the server runs the two agents as before.
+- *(all phases)* At the calibration, the conformance check's new weekly-scan rows: a project with a GitHub remote and no weekly workflow, or one whose lock-file list differs from the gate's, reads MISSING, which is configuration work in the next stage and reopens nothing; a project that will not run the scan records an inventory Decisions row beginning `Weekly scan:` with the reason, and reads a NOTE.
+- *(all phases)* A run-parameters file whose values the inventory check now finds empty (`RUN PARAMETERS: <key> is empty`) is rewritten with the five values on plain lines, in a records-only commit, and its header written again by `records-migrate.py`; nothing is asked of the owner that was not asked before.
+- *(all phases)* `invisible-check.py` may flag a file that passed under 2026.11.12a (a character of a category it did not read); the file is fixed in the next commit that touches it, never in a commit of its own.
+- *(all phases)* A key file that names `USERPROFILE`, `HOME`, `HOMEDRIVE`, `HOMEPATH`, `APPDATA` or `LOCALAPPDATA` is refused before the run: remove the line, since the strip sets those names itself; a tool that needs its state elsewhere is reported to the maintainer.
+- *(all phases)* Where `spec-packager` or `diff-reviewer` stops at its start naming a `mcp__context7__` tool after an update of Claude Code, the two names are taken off the two `tools:` lines by a hotfix of the bridge; a session without the server then sees both agents work as before. The symptom goes to the maintainer at once: without the two agents no brief is packaged and no Review A is started.
+- *(building, changing)* The round cause `base update`, for a re-read after the branch took its base, from the next numbered brief or review round.
+- *(building, changing)* `python ~/.claude/cursor-bridge/in-flight.py "<text>"` writes every entry of `run/supervisor/in-flight.md` from the next entry on, and `--pass <name> <reviewer> --round <n>` records a pass the guard does not open (Review A, an auditor, the short gate's read).
+- *(building, changing)* `python ~/.claude/cursor-bridge/review-guard.py ready <pr>` runs after the CI watch, before every merge, in every session that merges; the permission guard refuses a `gh pr merge` without its ready record, a pull request already past `premerge` at the install included. No merge is armed before the watch any more. The login that merges needs the right to read the branch's protection (a `CANNOT CHECK` names it); where `ready` refuses wrongly, the owner's own merge on GitHub is the way through, never a guard turned off.
+- *(building, changing)* `python ~/.claude/cursor-bridge/push-scan.py` runs before every push, in place of the hand-run `git log -p` scan.
+- *(building, changing)* A mutation run that ends with exit 5 had a test list failing unmutated: fix the test or its list, then run again; no kill counts from it.
+- *(building, changing)* A brief of one increment that no run has ended with exit 0, and that carries a `Merge unit:` line naming one ID or a header listing one, loses the line, where it has one, and reads `merge_unit: null` before its launch; a brief of a unit whose line or header names one increment only names them all; a brief with a completed run is left as it is and written as the next numbered brief, without the line, where it must be launched again.
+
+**If rolled back**
+- *(all phases)* `bridge-install.py --rollback` restores 2026.11.12a. The two programs this release adds leave with it, and with them their two allow entries, `Bash(python ~/.claude/cursor-bridge/in-flight.py:*)` and `Bash(python ~/.claude/cursor-bridge/push-scan.py:*)` (observed: the copy's settings hold both, the installed 2026.11.12a's neither): the in-flight log is written by hand again, and the pre-push scan is the hand-run `git log -p` of the older step 8.
+- *(all phases)* 2026.11.12a's programs read every record this release writes up to the stamp, observed on a scratch copy of this repository's records at eccc484, never the live records, with the installed programs: `inventory-check.py` `note: status: 28 lines / 10676 chars (cap 120 / 12000)` and `RESULT: OK`; `completion-check.py --mode plan` `note: mode plan; requirements: 102 built, 2 deferred, 1 planned` and `RESULT: OK`; `plan-check.py` `note: 84 increments in 1 file(s); 83 merged, 0 deferred` and `RESULT: OK`; `diagram-check.py --mode design` and `--mode code` and `workflow-check.py --status` `RESULT: OK`; `records-migrate.py --check` exit 0, every record `has a header` but the three merged briefs it reads `empty`, as before; `session-start.py` naming the phase's files as before; `trace-check.py` in its pinned mode `TRACED: 424 passages of baseline 0a186da; 123 in supervisor.md, 191 under workflow/, 0 dropped, 110 excused` and `RESULT: OK`. A project that calibrated to this release then records a `Bridge version:` newer than the installed one, which `/calibrate-bridge` reads as a release taken back and answers from `ROLLED-BACK.md`.
+- *(all phases)* `docs/TRACE_MOVES.md`, the ready records in a repository's git folder and the per-computer files `~/.cursor-bridge/projects.json` and `~/.cursor-bridge/names.txt` stay where they are and are read by nothing: the older `trace-check.py` refuses the mode (`unrecognized arguments: --moves`, exit 2), and the older `evaluate-reports.py`, `pace-report.py`, `review-guard.py` and `permission-guard.py` name neither file nor the ready folder. The evaluation's security section is written by hand again, as the older command says.
+- *(building, changing)* A merge needs the premerge record alone again: with the premerge record for a head and no ready record, the older permission guard's `merge_reason` for `gh pr merge 201 --squash --match-head-commit <head>` answered `None`, where this release's answers `gh pr merge for <head> without the ready record of pull request 201: run python ~/.claude/cursor-bridge/review-guard.py ready 201 after the CI watch`. The older step 8's hand-typed confirmation of CI comes back with it.
+- *(building, changing)* A `Round cause: base update` line is logged `unstated`, the older launcher's `round_cause` answering that the line names none of its seven causes; write a re-read after the branch took its base as `defect` or `records`, whichever the round's finding was. A `cause` in a rounds record is ignored: the older guard's `_validate_rounds_data` accepted a record whose entries carry one, refusing nothing.
+- *(design, planning, changing)* The plan critic goes back to its older pin, `model: claude-fable-5-1` in the installed definition, and rule 48 names Fable 5.1 again.
+- *(all phases)* `spec-packager` and `diff-reviewer` go back to `tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Write` and `tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash`, without the documentation server; the user-level Context7 setup stays and no bridge agent uses it.
+
+**Field acceptance**: on this repository, the first project to calibrate: the plan critic started once in the session after the install and reporting `claude-fable-5-2`; one increment merged with `ready` printing `READY` and the installed permission guard admitting the merge; `push-scan.py` before that push printing its clean line; `in-flight.py --pass` lines in the week's log and `pace-report.py` printing them; the first Sunday evaluation's `security` step writing this repository's and the TDP's sections from `~/.cursor-bridge/projects.json`, compared with each repository's Actions and Security pages. On the first other project to resume: the calibration's conformance rows and a lookup by `spec-packager` naming the version the project's lockfile pins. While no project has an increment at the gate, the demonstration on the stamped tree stands in.
+
+**For the maintainer**
+- The per-computer projects file, `~/.cursor-bridge/projects.json`, is written on every computer that runs the evaluation, before its next Sunday run, and its security step's window seeded once with `security --seed-from`.
+- The release procedure names the source tree's own `bridge-check.py --sources`, run from the tree it checks.
+- The run-sheet template carries the Context7 step for a first install, with the `claude` command's installation where it is missing.
+- Left for a later release, by name: the improvements release (the Sunday evaluations' items C25 to C61 and T44 to T108 and the pitfalls KP-084 to KP-100, C39 widened with T108, placed by the owner on 2026-11-22); pace-report's Started count reading CLOSE-, RECORDS- and REFAC-<stage> gate names as starts; the tests that take their week at import (`tests/test_task033_supervisor.py`); `cursor-configurator`'s missing `tools:` line; the weekly scan found by trigger in the conformance check and by file name in the evaluation; D-004's note on TASK-080's probe.
+
 ## 2026.11.12a
 
 **Release S, the slimming** (the maintainer's release, built in a separate clone on the owner's word of 2026-11-11 after the pace audit of 2026-11-09, its terms agreed with the bridge's supervisor on 2026-11-10; three pull requests through the full gate: the programs with their tests, the test retirements alone, the texts with this stamp): the loop sheds what cost rounds without catching defects, and nothing that caught one. The measure is the audit's: of the rounds of weeks 42 to 45, most went to wording pins, to records pull requests taking the whole gate, to whole-suite runs repeated per push and to re-reads after a compaction of text the step in hand never used. The programs that change: `bridge_env.py`, `bridge-run.py`, `cursor-agent.shim`, `bridge-check.py`, `bridge-install.py`, `completion-check.py`, `review-guard.py`, `session-start.py`, `plan-check.py` and `pace-report.py`. Against 2026.11.11a: no file new, none removed, no allow entry new (`review-guard.py premerge-records` runs on the guard's existing entry).
